{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters","id":1290395,"title":"Supporting Characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T09:39:34-08:00","id":1290395,"title":"Supporting Characters","content":"So I\u2019ve been going through Star Trek Adventures, the newest Trek RPG, and they have an interesting system for supporting characters. Basically the group has a pool of characters who are less skilled than the PCs, but still named. They\u2019re like the Reginald Barclays of the group. What you can do with them though is temporarily take control of them when it wouldn\u2019t make sense for your character to be in a scene or just couldn\u2019t contribute. Then you can switch back to your main character when they\u2019re in the spotlight and somebody else can do supporting character things. It also lets you spread out the party a bit more with some more PC control if you like.<br /> <br /> How does everyone think about this system working for Exalted, particularly with Allies and especially Retainers. In general Retainers represent people who are quite capable, but not nearly as powerful as your PC. Even powerful mortals would be fun to play if your Solar sorcerer needed a bodyguard, or your Dynast had a personal senechal to barter for her. With 5s in abilities and certain merits it wouldn\u2019t be so bad.<br /> <br /> Oh, also there\u2019s a limit on how many characters can be activated per mission, I\u2019d have to adapt that somehow. Maybe make it per story? That way you don\u2019t just spend some BP and have a young terrestrial who\u2019s perfect for any situation to take command of.<br /> <br /> So what d\u2019y\u2019all think? Good idea? Bad idea? Pitfalls I\u2019m not seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:56:55-08:00","id":1290407,"title":"","content":"We've done it a bit. It especially works for demons and stuff in combat. For example, when the sorceress got ambushed by the Wyld Hunt, I played Florivet, another player played Alveua, etc.<br /> <br /> And we've done it a bit for other stuff, like for example when the Djala tyrant does politics, another guy plays his priest. Gives them something to do.<br /> <br /> It's done on a bit of an ad-hoc basis though, might be better to be more formalised.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:17:11-08:00","id":1290415,"title":"","content":"Given the way my Okeanos game had supporting characters out the wazoo, I probably should have done something like this. But that game was sailing-focused, I can see more traditional games of Exalted not having quite enough of a cast to provide such a framework.<br /> <br /> \u200b(No, but seriously, the PCs started with <i>one</i> fully-crewed sailing ship, and moved into having <i>numerous</i> fully-crewed sailing ships.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-21-2019, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:43:35-08:00","id":1290427,"title":"","content":"We have a big cast, because each player is powerful and influential enough to have a bevy of associated NPCs, and they often pick up random extras.<br /> <br /> Not to mention we're having a conclave of the Cult of the Illuminated, so there's a whole bunch of Essence 2-3 Solars and Lunars who've turned up and are hanging around.<br /> <br /> They're just... well, NPCs. I guess there's an issue of consistency in how they're played, if sometimes the ST plays them and sometimes a PC plays them.<br /> (Not in combat though, it works fine for that, which is why the ST mostly uses it for combat.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T11:09:48-08:00","id":1290436,"title":"","content":"For some time now I've had an idea for a dynastic (and Dynastic) dragonblooded game where the PCs each control one elder and one young dragonblood. As time advanced, old PCs would be retired and new ones would be created as the young exalts of yesteryear became the new elders, and the long-term fortunes of the house take shape. I'm definitely not up to running two exalted games at once, though, so that'll have to be my next epic after my Abyssals game. Probably with some shorter games in between. <br /> <br /> Currently, I usually pass out the allied NPCs to players when they're involved in combat (assuming I don't just background them fighting a mook army while the PCs take on the Big Bad). But don't usually do it out of combat. I also give them opportunities to send parties of NPCs on missions and set their mission objectives and strategies, but those still play out in the background for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T12:10:14-08:00","id":1290475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290415#post1290415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the way my Okeanos game had supporting characters out the wazoo, I probably should have done something like this. But that game was sailing-focused, I can see more traditional games of Exalted not having quite enough of a cast to provide such a framework.<br /> <br /> \u200b(No, but seriously, the PCs started with <i>one</i> fully-crewed sailing ship, and moved into having <i>numerous</i> fully-crewed sailing ships.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really fun but a bookkeeping nightmare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290427#post1290427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're just... well, NPCs. I guess there's an issue of consistency in how they're played, if sometimes the ST plays them and sometimes a PC plays them.<br /> (Not in combat though, it works fine for that, which is why the ST mostly uses it for combat.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that\u2019s why it works best with Retainers, since they\u2019re close to the PCs and will tend most to act in their best interest anyway. It might also be important to give them a small amount of strong character traits, possibly butting up against exaggeration, so they can stay consistent. Like a bodyguard who\u2019s bound by honour and duty and that\u2019s about it. So if the PCs ever enter a situation where they\u2019re trying to lie she might object to the dishonourable tactics or something, unless her master is there.<br /> <br /> The supporting cast shouldn\u2019t be TOO interesting anyway, otherwise they would be main characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:21:59-08:00","id":1290583,"title":"","content":"Ars Magica had a system very much like that. They called it &quot;troupe style&quot; play. The idea was that the Covenant (the organization of Magi, analogous to a Circle, Brotherhood, or guild of some sort) was the shared character that grew over the course of the Chronicle. <br /> <br /> Time was broken out into seasons, so you might have a season's quest be undertaken by one or two Magi and their retainers. You might have a shield bearer, a thief, and an archer along, chosen from the retinue of the Covenant. Retainers were expressly less powerful than Magi ('cause this is Ars Magica) and somewhat interchangeable if they had casualties or just needed to swap out for a scene. <br /> <br /> The other Magi might be on their own quests, or staying home brewing up potions and doing research.<br /> <br /> I thought it was a magnificent idea. My players didn't, so that was the end of Ars for us. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I did keep the ideas in mind though, and we've occasionally had character swaps that worked out much better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T16:26:56-08:00","id":1290586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290475#post1290475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The supporting cast shouldn\u2019t be TOO interesting anyway, otherwise they would be main characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe!<br /> <br /> On the other hand, main characters can have very long storylines and deeply set habits. Swapping off for an evening also brings the freedom to cut loose and play that supporting character way over the top.<br /> <br /> What would <i>you</i> do, if you were playing a trooper in your Solar Lord's retinue, it was your last day before retirement, when suddenly the outposts beyond the castle are clanging their alarm gongs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:35:10-08:00","id":1290735,"title":"","content":"The manor worry I see for a supporting character idea like this is that, at least in my group, the major draw is the rp, which means character traits and personality, obviously. And everyone plays and comes at things a little differently, obviously, so the idea of a shared character sort of seems like it might end up with two people playing the same character with marked differences, or different from how they play as an NPC. This could be troublesome in some ways, as people find NPCs they like having suddenly different personalities or similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:40:47-08:00","id":1290738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290735#post1290735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The manor worry I see for a supporting character idea like this is that, at least in my group, the major draw is the rp, which means character traits and personality, obviously. And everyone plays and comes at things a little differently, obviously, so the idea of a shared character sort of seems like it might end up with two people playing the same character with marked differences, or different from how they play as an NPC. This could be troublesome in some ways, as people find NPCs they like having suddenly different personalities or similar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that's definitely something to keep an eye on, certainly in my group while we have people play NPCs a little bit, on random occasion, any character that builds real personality tends to consistently be picked up by the same player, so Boros, the Dawn Caste's sycophantic high priest is generally played by one dude, whereas Loros, Boros's arch-rival and the Dawn Caste's sniveling seneschal is played by another. And of course care has to be taken that they don't steal the scene from the actual PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T08:55:47-08:00","id":1290788,"title":"","content":"I've played a lot of Ars Magica and in my games it has been pretty common for the companions (the less powerful characters) to be more loved than the magi (the more powerful ones). To me saying that they shouldn't be too interesting doesn't make sense. They should be as Interesting as possible.<br /> <br /> There is a third level of character (the grog) who are about as powerful as companions but can't have story flaws (the sort of character traits that you plot stories around) they're not designed to be the center of the story. Yet when they've become interesting we've never balked at telling stories around them. Role playing is improvisational, we roll with the punches and abandon plan A all of the time.<br /> <br /> Exalts are similar to Ars Magica magi in that they stand head and shoulders above most of the rest of the setting and their character generation rules tend to create really interesting and fun characters. I wouldn't be too concerned about having your Exalted become sidelined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 02-22-2019, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:47:23-08:00","id":1290805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290788#post1290788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played a lot of Ars Magica and in my games it has been pretty common for the companions (the less powerful characters) to be more loved than the magi (the more powerful ones). To me saying that they shouldn't be too interesting doesn't make sense. They should be as Interesting as possible.<br /> <br /> There is a third level of character (the grog) who are about as powerful as companions but can't have story flaws (the sort of character traits that you plot stories around) they're not designed to be the center of the story. Yet when they've become interesting we've never balked at telling stories around them. Role playing is improvisational, we roll with the punches and abandon plan A all of the time.<br /> <br /> Exalts are similar to Ars Magi magi in that they stand head and shoulders above most of the rest of the setting and their character generation rules tend to create really interesting and fun characters. I wouldn't be too concerned about having your Exalted become sidelined.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that\u2019s true, but at that point why are you playing the Solars at all at that point? You can just play just play the mortals or DB supporting cast as main characters. <br /> <br /> My point was more if you\u2019re way more invested in a side character who you\u2019ve put a lot more effort and time into then they shouldn\u2019t really be one of the filler people anymore. Also as an ST it puts a lot of undo stress on me to have PCs constantly swapping the character they want to have as their main character. That kept happening to me in the last campaign I ran and it was maddening. Like one character would include in her backstory that she lost a sister long ago and by the time they\u2019d found out she was alive and the current leader of a group of southern raiders her sister wouldn\u2019t be in the party anymore, but there WOULD be a character who had an ancient fire elemental in her family tree. They taught her martial arts, and there was a storyline where the elemental\u2019s dojo got attacked by a jealous former student-turned rival, except right at the beginning she was gone and another guy was there in her place who had something else completely going on. <br /> <br /> Changing characters is cool a lot of the time, but if I\u2019m going to put in a lot of work to weave your character\u2019s personal backstory into the over arching narrative and the narratives of other PC backstories it really helps to know at least a week or two in advance who you\u2019ll be playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:31:00-08:00","id":1290846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290805#post1290805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point was more if you\u2019re way more invested in a side character who you\u2019ve put a lot more effort and time into then they shouldn\u2019t really be one of the filler people anymore. Also as an ST it puts a lot of undo stress on me to have PCs constantly swapping the character they want to have as their main character. That kept happening to me in the last campaign I ran and it was maddening. Like one character would include in her backstory that she lost a sister long ago and by the time they\u2019d found out she was alive and the current leader of a group of southern raiders her sister wouldn\u2019t be in the party anymore, but there WOULD be a character who had an ancient fire elemental in her family tree. They taught her martial arts, and there was a storyline where the elemental\u2019s dojo got attacked by a jealous former student-turned rival, except right at the beginning she was gone and another guy was there in her place who had something else completely going on.<br /> <br /> Changing characters is cool a lot of the time, but if I\u2019m going to put in a lot of work to weave your character\u2019s personal backstory into the over arching narrative and the narratives of other PC backstories it really helps to know at least a week or two in advance who you\u2019ll be playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things can be easier with a flexible cast of characters. <br /> <br /> I've found my players less likely to want to switch PC's if they can get a break from being &quot;angry fire mage&quot; every session. <br /> <br /> The players shouldn't choose characters in a vacuum. If I want to run a murder mystery game I speak with the players whose wizards can read the memories of everyone they come in contact with or summon up the ghosts of the dead for a discussion to establish what else they're doing that will keep them solving the mystery in 20 seconds. Having a flexible cast gives you more hooks to hang stories on and allows you to get what the group thinks are the most fun characters for each particular story. It makes running a game easier not harder.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:23:18-08:00","id":1290871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apromor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1290395-supporting-characters?p=1290846#post1290846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These things can be easier with a flexible cast of characters. <br /> <br /> I've found my players less likely to want to switch PC's if they can get a break from being &amp;quot;angry fire mage&amp;quot; every session. <br /> <br /> The players shouldn't choose characters in a vacuum. If I want to run a murder mystery game I speak with the players whose wizards can read the memories of everyone they come in contact with or summon up the ghosts of the dead for a discussion to establish what else they're doing that will keep them solving the mystery in 20 seconds. Having a flexible cast gives you more hooks to hang stories on and allows you to get what the group thinks are the most fun characters for each particular story. It makes running a game easier not harder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that could help. Part of my frustration on the matter is in that campaign I was designing super awesome artifacts for everyone, every time a player was like \u201cI hate that my class doesn\u2019t have a good ranged option to fight flying enemies.\u201d I\u2019d rush to jot down \u201cinclude ranged attack or fast flight option.\u201d On the artifact work in progress page. Also this whole time since the artifacts were coming from particular powerful gods who had taken an interest in them i was compiling a list of all the things they\u2019d done within the perview. So one of them had, basically from the first session, taken every resource he could and used it to revitalize collapsed villages and dead woods, and he was the one that the god of nature\u2019s bounty and growth had taken a liking to.<br /> <br /> Anyway without going on too long the culmination like 3/4 of the way through the campaign was each person getting this big meeting with a powerful and ancient spirit who was custom tailored to make them reflect upon all they had personally accomplished, followed by artifacts that gave them everything they ever wished their character could do and more. It was like watching your kids on Christmas morning getting the most awesome gifts. Except for one, who I felt awful about because I had like six half finished artifacts for previous characters, and different incarnations of his current one. <br /> <br /> And again I\u2019m totally cool with swapping characters, I made this whole thread for swapping in ensemble cast characters, I even think it would be fun to play a game where nobody had any character at all in particular and everyone just picked one on a whim from a pool at the start of each session. That being said, there are reasons why you might want a smaller and more focused group of main characters with ones who are firmly, but not strictly, going to be relegated to support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T19:59:39-08:00","id":1291404,"title":"","content":"In our all-too-short Ars game, we had a shield-bearer companion who was too poor at chargen to afford a shield, so he had a chain shirt he held stretched out like a kite. <br /> <br /> We also abused the Merits and Flaws system to create an immortal thief. Immortality didn't grant immunity to the Decrepitude system, so he had an absurd number of points in skills for stealing, and also was too decrepit to move. We decided that he was basically a big bowl of sand, and now and then items would just appear in the sand after being lost. We didn't play this guy, but he does show up as a funny reference now and then in other games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Character swapping is a feature in our current Chronicle. We're setting up our Solars as the ones who jump into the various Aeons (pocket dimensions, basically) to deal with the forces that dwell there. Our DBs are the ones who are getting the role for protecting Creation and the mortals, dealing with the politics and intrigue. We've even had some fun scenes with the Circle and Brotherhood meeting each other and having a social scene, with my four players splitting up two by two to deal with both sides of the discussion. <br /> <br /> Good times. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}